---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Editorial policy of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: sources, fixes`} description="Which USCIS pages and lists Citizenship Test Free relies on, how its practice answer choices are written, which sources it refuses and how a mistake is corrected and dated." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Editorial policy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Editorial and corrections policy</h1>
    <p>People use these pages to decide when to file Form N-400 and how much to pay. A stale fee or a wrong day limit can cost them a refused application, so every figure points back to the official page it was read on.</p>
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2><p>{AUTHOR_NAME}, reachable at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    <h2>What we read</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>USCIS: the 2025 and 2008 civics question lists, the test updates page, the reading and writing vocabulary lists and the study pages;</li>
      <li>the Form N-400 page and its instructions, the fee rule, Form I-912 and the poverty guidelines table used for the reduced fee;</li>
      <li>the USCIS Policy Manual, volume 12, on continuous residence, physical presence, the English and civics tests and the oath, and the USCIS processing time data.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How the questions are written</h2><p>The civics questions and the accepted answers are the official USCIS lists, copied without change. We write the three wrong choices of each practice question and the English practice sentences ourselves, from the official vocabulary. We never copy from an app, a book or another practice site.</p>
    <h2>Sources we refuse</h2><p>Law firms, immigration consultants, app publishers and practice sites never supply a figure here. A rule we cannot find on an official page is not published.</p>
    <h2>Review cycle</h2><p>A script compares the N-400 fees on uscis.gov with our parameter file every month. The question lists and rules are re-read when USCIS announces a change, and the answers that depend on current officeholders are checked against the USCIS test updates page. Every page shows the date of the last check.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <ol><li>We open the official page again.</li><li>We correct the parameter file or the question and add a test for the case.</li><li>The site rebuilds and shows the new date.</li></ol>
    <h2>Independence</h2><p>No law firm, adviser, publisher or government pays for or reviews what is published here, and the site carries no affiliate link. See also the <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a>. Version: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
